ustries  require different incentives it only  makes sense to negotiate individually  why should the inventor of a Buy Now  button be granted just as long a  monopoly as the creator of a drug that  took years and years of research the  solution is a prize system where the  first inventor gets a check not a  monopoly this way companies compete  lower prices and make their products  more accessible not in 20 years when  their patent expires but today many new  companies would finally have a fighting  chance and as a nice cherry on top  patent trolls would be eliminated  overnight of course there are some  challenges we need a system for  determining what kind of inventions  require a prize and that money would  have to come from somewhere which  probably means your favorite higher  taxes again it's not perfect but it need  only be 1% better than what we have and  that's already a pretty low bar so if  such a simple solution exists why aren't  we using it for one because the  companies that benefit most from patents  are the ones with money to lobby for  them and because many people just don't  know much about economics there just  isn't much awareness but patents and the  stock market are really economic games  and with today's sponsor brilliant you  can learn the hidden mathematical rules  to better understand them  it teaches concepts like game theory  economic statistics and tons of other  topics on science math and computer  science unlike your professor brilliant  understands that people learn by doing  not just memorizing over and over again  so you'll solve riddles play with graphs  and answer challenges as you progress  through the lessons to get started or  dive deeper into the world of math  science and technology go to brilliant  org slash poly matter and sign up today  for free the first 200 people to use  that link will also get 20% off at the  annual premium subscription thanks to  brilliant for sponsoring this video and  as always to you for listening
 

